{"The mapping between error IDs and nodestore data is incorrect when some events are cached or missing, because it zips the ordered error_ids list with events.values(), whose order can differ from the original node ID list, causing error titles/messages to be attributed to the wrong IDs": 0.9689998030662537, "When the feature flag is enabled, the new table visualization is rendered with empty columns and table data instead of the actual result data, so users will see a blank table despite having query results": 0.998723566532135, "When the query is disabled (e.g., feature flag off), the hook can return with isPending and isError both false while data is still undefined, so the final return path that reads properties from data will throw at runtime": 0.9624063372612, "The override header cell renderer treats any falsy ReactNode (like 0 or an empty string) as 'no value' and falls back to the default renderer, so valid cell content can be silently replaced": 0.9644319415092468, "The override body cell renderer also uses a generic truthy check, causing valid falsy ReactNode values (e.g. 0) to be discarded and replaced with the default cell": 0.9776723980903625, "The regex filter for attribute keys only allows bare keys or tags[key,number] format, so keys like tags[sentry.message.*] that isKnownAttribute explicitly intends to include are silently filtered out": 0.8617055416107178, "The direct HTTP call to Snuba in the test helper has no timeout, so if the Snuba endpoint is slow or hangs, the entire test run can block indefinitely instead of failing fast": 0.7517111897468567}